From: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:42:58 +1000
Subject: pmdomain: sun55i-pck600: Fix NULL pointer dereference and ensure domains on

Fix a NULL pointer dereference panic in sunxi_pck600_probe() and ensure probed
power domains are powered on and marked GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON.

In the original sun55i-pck600 driver, sunxi_pck600_probe() invoked
sunxi_pck600_pd_set_power() before initializing pd->pck, resulting in an
immediate NULL pointer dereference kernel panic during early boot. Assigning
pd->pck = pck prior to power state initialization resolves the crash.

Additionally, marking registered domains with GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON prevents
generic power domain idle sweeps from powering down hardware power islands
that contain in-use or un-probed peripherals.

Signed-off-by: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Assisted-by: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>

---
diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
index 1d47bbd35..d7931bad2 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
@@ -176,6 +176,9 @@ static int sunxi_pck600_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		pd->genpd.power_on = sunxi_pck600_power_on;
 		pd->genpd.flags = pd_desc->flags;
 		pd->base = base + PPU_REG_SIZE * i;
+		pd->pck = pck;
 
 		sunxi_pck600_pd_setup(pd, desc);
+		sunxi_pck600_pd_set_power(pd, true);
+		pd->genpd.flags |= GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON;
 		ret = pm_genpd_init(&pd->genpd, NULL, false);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to initialize power domain\n");
